       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Requested:** metformin 1700 mg PO TID, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as 850 mg TID. Extended-release is capped at 2,000 mg/day. The most a single dose should be is about 1,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** The requested daily dose is twice the maximum. That raises the risk of severe GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 850 mg PO TID with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,000 mg PO BID with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- 500 mg PO TID with meals (1,500 mg/day)\n- Another dose or formulation\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If 1700 mg TID is what you intended, tell me and I can enter it with a note documenting that it exceeds the maximum dose. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
