     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order as written. I know you've confirmed it. But 5,100 mg/day is twice the maximum labeled dose, and I can't think of a clinical situation where that's appropriate. It carries a real risk of serious harm, mainly lactic acidosis, and it won't improve glycemic control. Higher doses add little benefit beyond about 2,000 mg/day.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within range now.** For example, 850 mg PO TID with meals, or 1,000 mg PO BID with meals. I can add a note that you plan to titrate.\n- **Hold the order while you check.** Pharmacy or your attending can confirm the intended dose. If the 1700 mg figure came from a transcription slip, an extended-release product, or a different drug, it's better to catch that now.\n\nIf you tell me which dose you'd like, I'll enter it right away."
      }
